{"id":"9866155f79fa5a7c","subject":"go:golang.org/x/net","time":"2026-09-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.59.0"},"statement":"`golang.org/x/net/quic.Stream.StopSending(code uint64)` aborts reads and unblocks pending reads, sends the application error code to the peer without waiting for acknowledgment, and is valid only for codes less than 2^62; it returns an error when called on a write-only stream. For example, `err := stream.StopSending(42)` requests termination of the peer's sending direction.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/net/+/v0.59.0/quic/stream.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:42.401646815Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"57230d47c3fb1df5","subject":"go:golang.org/x/net","time":"2026-10-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.60.0"},"statement":"golang.org/x/net/http2 hardens its server against HPACK encoder races that could crash the process; callers serving HTTP/2 no longer encounter that race-triggered panic from concurrent header encoding.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/net/+/v0.60.0/http2/server.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:22:48.857786145Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ba4a984287550200","subject":"go:golang.org/x/net","time":"2026-02-09T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"0.50.0"},"statement":"In v0.50.0, `http2` provides `Framer.WritePriorityUpdate` and support for processing RFC 9218 priorities on the server, but its client `Transport` does not turn a request’s `Priority` header into a `PRIORITY_UPDATE` frame. Setting `req.Header.Set(\"Priority\", \"u=1\")` sends the header as a request header; it does not make the transport communicate the priority in a `PRIORITY_UPDATE` frame.","source":"https://go.googlesource.com/net/+/v0.50.0/http2/transport.go","added":"2026-10-25T20:23:55.674048018Z","by":"agent"}
